{"id":"f1d70435cd487e3e03fda694f0df77ee3274d458","axis":"silent","repo":"ckeditor/ckeditor5","sha":"f1d70435cd487e3e03fda694f0df77ee3274d458","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changelog/20260911131617_ck_11390.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@","+---","+type: Fix","+scope:","+  - ckeditor5-engine","+  - ckeditor5-utils","+  - ckeditor5-paste-from-office","+  - ckeditor5-html-support","+---","+","+Processing instructions in the input data no longer cause an error during conversion.","+","+Browsers have started parsing `<?target data?>` markup in HTML into processing instruction nodes rather than comments. Such nodes are now ignored by default, consistently with how comments have always been handled. Data processors expose a new `skipProcessingInstructions` flag for integrations that need to preserve them."],"additions":12,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/ckeditor5-engine/manual/processing-instruction.manual.html","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,122 @@","+<!doctype html>","+<html lang=\"en\">","+\t<head>","+\t\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\" />","+\t\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />","+\t\t<title>Processing instructions</title>","+\t\t<script type=\"module\" src=\"./processing-instruction.ts\"></script>","+\t</head>","+\t<body>","+\t\t<ck-manual-header>","+\t\t\t<h3>Requirements</h3>","+\t\t\t<p>","+\t\t\t\tThis test needs a browser that parses <code>&#x3C;?target data?&#x3E;</code> in HTML","+\t\t\t\tinto processing instruction nodes. Engines without that support parse the same markup","+\t\t\t\tinto comments, so nothing below will be visible &#x2013; that is expected, not a","+\t\t\t\tfailure. To check, run in the console:","+\t\t\t</p>","+\t\t\t<pre>new DOMParser().parseFromString( '&#x3C;body&#x3E;&#x3C;?foo bar?&#x3E;&#x3C;/body&#x3E;', 'text/html' ).body.firstChild.nodeType === 7</pre>","+","+\t\t\t<h3>Loading</h3>","+\t\t\t<ol>","+\t\t\t\t<li>","+\t\t\t\t\tThe editor should load without any error in the console. This alone covers the","+\t\t\t\t\toriginal problem, where a processing instruction reached the converter and had no","+\t\t\t\t\t<code>tagName</code>.","+\t\t\t\t</li>","+\t\t\t\t<li>","+\t\t\t\t\tThe first paragraph should show two yellow boxes,","+\t\t\t\t\t<code>&#x3C;?marker start?&#x3E;</code> and <code>&#x3C;?marker end?&#x3E;</code>,","+\t\t\t\t\taround the words \"between the markers\".","+\t\t\t\t</li>","+\t\t\t\t<li>","+\t\t\t\t\tThe second paragraph should show <code>&#x3C;?if !supportLists?&#x3E;</code>,","+\t\t\t\t\tthe third one <code>&#x3C;?endif?&#x3E;</code> with no data part.","+\t\t\t\t</li>","+\t\t\t\t<li>","+\t\t\t\t\tThe output below should repeat the source markup, with the instructions in the","+\t\t\t\t\tsame positions relative to the text.","+\t\t\t\t</li>","+\t\t\t</ol>","+","+\t\t\t<h3>Testing</h3>","+\t\t\t<ol>","+\t\t\t\t<li>","+\t\t\t\t\tType text before, between and after the boxes, then press","+\t\t\t\t\t<strong>Print data</strong>. The instructions should stay in place relative to","+\t\t\t\t\tthe surrounding text.","+\t\t\t\t</li>","+\t\t\t\t<li>","+\t\t\t\t\tPlace the caret right after a box and press <kbd>Backspace</kbd>. The whole","+\t\t\t\t\tinstruction should be removed and should disappear from the output.","+\t\t\t\t</li>","+\t\t\t\t<li>","+\t\t\t\t\tUndo the removal. The instruction should come back with the same target and data.","+\t\t\t\t</li>","+\t\t\t\t<li>","+\t\t\t\t\tSelect a range covering one box and some text, then type over it. Only that","+\t\t\t\t\tinstruction should be gone from the output.","+\t\t\t\t</li>","+\t\t\t\t<li>","+\t\t\t\t\tPress <strong>Reset data</strong> at any point to load the source markup again.","+\t\t\t\t</li>","+\t\t\t\t<li>","+\t\t\t\t\tApply bold to text spanning a box. The instruction should survive and stay in the","+\t\t\t\t\toutput.","+\t\t\t\t</li>","+\t\t\t</ol>","+","+\t\t\t<p>Known limitations of this demo:</p>","+\t\t\t<ul>","+\t\t\t\t<li>","+\t\t\t\t\tThe instruction is rendered as a plain UI element, not a widget, so it cannot be","+\t\t\t\t\tselected by clicking. This keeps the test free of a dependency on","+\t\t\t\t\t<code>ckeditor5-widget</code>.","+\t\t\t\t</li>","+\t\t\t\t<li>","+\t\t\t\t\tCopying and pasting an instruction does not preserve it. The clipboard uses its","+\t\t\t\t\town data processor instance, which still skips processing instructions.","+\t\t\t\t</li>","+\t\t\t\t<li>","+\t\t\t\t\tData containing <code>&#x3E;</code> is not handled. A processing instruction ends","+\t\t\t\t\tat the first <code>&#x3E;</code> and there is no escaping, so such data would not","+\t\t\t\t\tsurvive a round trip.","+\t\t\t\t</li>","+\t\t\t</ul>","+\t\t</ck-manual-header>","+","+\t\t<style>","+\t\t\tbody {","+\t\t\t\tfont-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;","+\t\t\t\tfont-size: 14px;","+\t\t\t}","+","+\t\t\t.ck-content .processing-instruction {","+\t\t\t\tbackground: #fff3c4;","+\t\t\t\tborder: 1px solid #e0c060;","+\t\t\t\tborder-radius: 3px;","+\t\t\t\tpadding: 0 4px;","+\t\t\t\tfont-family: monospace;","+\t\t\t\tfont-size: 0.9em;","+\t\t\t\twhite-space: nowrap;","+\t\t\t}","+","+\t\t\t#data-output {","+\t\t\t\tbackground: #f4f4f4;","+\t\t\t\tborder: 1px solid #ddd;","+\t\t\t\tpadding: 10px;","+\t\t\t\twhite-space: pre-wrap;","+\t\t\t\tword-break: break-word;","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t</style>","+","+\t\t<div id=\"editor\"></div>","+","+\t\t<p>","+\t\t\t<button id=\"print-data\" type=\"button\">Print data</button>","+\t\t\t<button id=\"reset-data\" type=\"button\">Reset data</button>","+\t\t</p>","+","+\t\t<pre id=\"data-output\"></pre>","+\t</body>","+</html>"],"additions":122,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/ckeditor5-engine/manual/processing-instruction.ts","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,133 @@","+/**","+ * @license Copyright (c) 2003-2026, CKSource Holding sp. z o.o. All rights reserved.","+ * For licensing, see LICENSE.md or https://ckeditor.com/legal/ckeditor-licensing-options","+ */","+","+import { ClassicEditor } from '@ckeditor/ckeditor5-editor-classic';","+import { Enter } from '@ckeditor/ckeditor5-enter';","+import { Typing } from '@ckeditor/ckeditor5-typing';","+import { Paragraph } from '@ckeditor/ckeditor5-paragraph';","+import { Bold, Italic } from '@ckeditor/ckeditor5-basic-styles';","+import { Undo } from '@ckeditor/ckeditor5-undo';","+","+import type { UpcastElementEvent } from '../src/conversion/upcastdispatcher.js';","+","+declare global {","+\tinterface Window { editor: any }","+}","+","+// Kept as a string rather than in the page markup on purpose. Whether `<?target data?>` in the page","+// source is parsed into a processing instruction depends on the browser, and the converters below are","+// registered only after `create()` resolves - so the initial content has to be set explicitly anyway.","+const INITIAL_DATA =","+\t'<p>Paired markers: <?marker start?>between the markers<?marker end?> and done.</p>' +","+\t'<p>A list marker follows: <?if !supportLists?>1.</p>' +","+\t'<p>An instruction with no data part: <?endif?></p>';","+","+/**","+ * Custom properties come back as `unknown`, and a processing instruction ends at the first `>`","+ * with no way to escape it - so anything that would not survive a round trip is dropped here.","+ */","+function readProperty( viewElement: { getCustomProperty( name: string ): unknown }, name: string ): string {","+\tconst value = viewElement.getCustomProperty( name );","+","+\tif ( typeof value !== 'string' || value.includes( '>' ) ) {","+\t\treturn '';","+\t}","+","+\treturn value;","+}","+","+ClassicEditor","+\t.create( {","+\t\tattachTo: document.querySelector( '#editor' ) as HTMLElement,","+\t\tplugins: [ Enter, Typing, Paragraph, Bold, Italic, Undo ],","+\t\ttoolbar: [ 'bold', 'italic', '|', 'undo', 'redo' ]","+\t} )","+\t.then( editor => {","+\t\twindow.editor = editor;","+","+\t\t// By default the data processor drops processing instructions, exactly like comments.","+\t\t// They have to reach the view before any converter can see them.","+\t\teditor.data.processor.skipProcessingInstructions = false;","+","+\t\teditor.model.schema.register( 'processingInstruction', {","+\t\t\tinheritAllFrom: '$inlineObject',","+\t\t\tallowAttributes: [ 'piTarget', 'piData' ]","+\t\t} );","+","+\t\t// View `$processingInstruction` UI element -> model element.","+\t\teditor.conversion.for( 'upcast' ).add( dispatcher => {","+\t\t\tdispatcher.on<UpcastElementEvent>( 'element:$processingInstruction', ( evt, data, conversionApi ) => {","+\t\t\t\tif ( !conversionApi.consumable.consume( data.viewItem, { name: true } ) ) {","+\t\t\t\t\treturn;","+\t\t\t\t}","+","+\t\t\t\tconst target = readProperty( data.viewItem, '$processingTarget' );","+","+\t\t\t\tif ( !target ) {","+\t\t\t\t\treturn;","+\t\t\t\t}","+","+\t\t\t\tconst modelElement = conversionApi.writer.createElement( 'processingInstruction', {","+\t\t\t\t\tpiTarget: target,","+\t\t\t\t\tpiData: readProperty( data.viewItem, '$processingData' )","+\t\t\t\t} );","+","+\t\t\t\tif ( !conversionApi.safeInsert( modelElement, data.modelCursor ) ) {","+\t\t\t\t\treturn;","+\t\t\t\t}","+","+\t\t\t\tconversionApi.updateConversionResult( modelElement, data );","+\t\t\t} );","+\t\t} );","+","+\t\t// Model element -> a real processing instruction node in the output data. The UI element name","+\t\t// is what makes the DOM converter call `createProcessingInstruction()` instead of `createElement()`.","+\t\teditor.conversion.for( 'dataDowncast' ).elementToElement( {","+\t\t\tmodel: 'processingInstruction',","+\t\t\tview: ( modelElement, { writer } ) => {","+\t\t\t\tconst viewElement = writer.createUIElement( '$processingInstruction' );","+","+\t\t\t\twriter.setCustomProperty( '$processingTarget', modelElement.getAttribute( 'piTarget' ), viewElement );","+\t\t\t\twriter.setCustomProperty( '$processingData', modelElement.getAttribute( 'piData' ), viewElement );","+","+\t\t\t\treturn viewElement;","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t} );","+","+\t\t// Model element -> something visible, so the instruction can be located and deleted.","+\t\teditor.conversion.for( 'editingDowncast' ).elementToElement( {","+\t\t\tmodel: 'processingInstruction',","+\t\t\tview: ( modelElement, { writer } ) => {","+\t\t\t\tconst target = modelElement.getAttribute( 'piTarget' );","+\t\t\t\tconst data = modelElement.getAttribute( 'piData' );","+\t\t\t\tconst label = data ? `<?${ target } ${ data }?>` : `<?${ target }?>`;","+","+\t\t\t\treturn writer.createUIElement( 'span', { class: 'processing-instruction' }, function( domDocument ) {","+\t\t\t\t\tconst domElement = this.toDomElement( domDocument );","+","+\t\t\t\t\tdomElement.textContent = label;","+","+\t\t\t\t\treturn domElement;","+\t\t\t\t} );","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t} );","+","+\t\teditor.setData( INITIAL_DATA );","+\t\tprintData();","+","+\t\tdocument.getElementById( 'print-data' )!.addEventListener( 'click', printData );","+","+\t\tdocument.getElementById( 'reset-data' )!.addEventListener( 'click', () => {","+\t\t\teditor.setData( INITIAL_DATA );","+\t\t\tprintData();","+\t\t} );","+","+\t\tfunction printData() {","+\t\t\tdocument.getElementById( 'data-output' )!.textContent = editor.getData();","+\t\t}","+\t} )","+\t.catch( err => {","+\t\tconsole.error( err.stack );","+\t} );"],"additions":133,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/ckeditor5-engine/src/dataprocessor/dataprocessor.ts","lines":["@@ -67,4 +67,10 @@ export interface DataProcessor {"," \t * If `false`, comment nodes will be converted to `$comment`. Otherwise comment nodes are ignored."," \t */"," \tskipComments?: boolean;","+","+\t/**","+\t * If `false`, processing instruction nodes (for example `<?target data?>`) will be converted.","+\t * Otherwise, processing instruction nodes are ignored.","+\t */","+\tskipProcessingInstructions?: boolean;"," }"],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/ckeditor5-engine/src/dataprocessor/htmldataprocessor.ts","lines":["@@ -38,8 +38,21 @@ export class HtmlDataProcessor implements DataProcessor {"," \t */"," \tpublic htmlWriter: DataProcessorHtmlWriter;"," ","+\t/**","+\t * If `false`, comment nodes will be converted. Otherwise, comment nodes are ignored.","+\t *","+\t * @default true","+\t */"," \tpublic skipComments: boolean = true;"," ","+\t/**","+\t * If `false`, processing instruction nodes (for example `<?target data?>`) will be converted.","+\t * Otherwise, processing instruction nodes are ignored.","+\t *","+\t * @default true","+\t */","+\tpublic skipProcessingInstructions: boolean = true;","+"," \t/**"," \t * Creates a new instance of the HTML data processor class."," \t *","@@ -76,7 +89,10 @@ export class HtmlDataProcessor implements DataProcessor {"," \t\tconst domFragment = this._toDom( data );"," "," \t\t// Convert DOM DocumentFragment to view DocumentFragment.","-\t\treturn this.domConverter.domToView( domFragment, { skipComments: this.skipComments } ) as ViewDocumentFragment;","+\t\treturn this.domConverter.domToView( domFragment, {","+\t\t\tskipComments: this.skipComments,","+\t\t\tskipProcessingInstructions: this.skipProcessingInstructions","+\t\t} ) as ViewDocumentFragment;"," \t}"," "," \t/**"],"additions":17,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/ckeditor5-engine/src/dataprocessor/xmldataprocessor.ts","lines":["@@ -49,8 +49,21 @@ export class XmlDataProcessor implements DataProcessor {"," \t */"," \tpublic htmlWriter: DataProcessorHtmlWriter;"," ","+\t/**","+\t * If `false`, comment nodes will be converted. Otherwise, comment nodes are ignored.","+\t *","+\t * @default true","+\t */"," \tpublic skipComments: boolean = true;"," ","+\t/**","+\t * If `false`, processing instruction nodes (for example `<?target data?>`) will be converted.","+\t * Otherwise, processing instruction nodes are ignored.","+\t *","+\t * @default true","+\t */","+\tpublic skipProcessingInstructions: boolean = true;","+"," \t/**"," \t * Creates a new instance of the XML data processor class."," \t *","@@ -95,7 +108,8 @@ export class XmlDataProcessor implements DataProcessor {"," \t\t\tdomFragment,"," \t\t\t{"," \t\t\t\tkeepOriginalCase: true,","-\t\t\t\tskipComments: this.skipComments","+\t\t\t\tskipComments: this.skipComments,","+\t\t\t\tskipProcessingInstructions: this.skipProcessingInstructions"," \t\t\t}"," \t\t) as ViewDocumentFragment;"," \t}"],"additions":15,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/ckeditor5-engine/src/view/domconverter.ts","lines":["@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@ import {"," \ttype ShadowSelection,"," \tisText,"," \tisComment,","+\tisProcessingInstruction,"," \tisValidAttributeName,"," \tfirst,"," \tgetParentElement,","@@ -447,7 +448,12 @@ export class ViewDomConverter {"," \t\t\t\t\tthis.bindDocumentFragments( domElement, viewElementOrFragment );"," \t\t\t\t}"," \t\t\t} else if ( viewElementOrFragment.is( 'uiElement' ) ) {","-\t\t\t\tif ( viewElementOrFragment.name === '$comment' ) {","+\t\t\t\tif ( viewElementOrFragment.name === '$processingInstruction' ) {","+\t\t\t\t\tdomElement = this._domDocument.createProcessingInstruction(","+\t\t\t\t\t\tviewElementOrFragment.getCustomProperty( '$processingTarget' ) as string,","+\t\t\t\t\t\tviewElementOrFragment.getCustomProperty( '$processingData' ) as string","+\t\t\t\t\t);","+\t\t\t\t} else if ( viewElementOrFragment.name === '$comment' ) {"," \t\t\t\t\tdomElement = this._domDocument.createComment( viewElementOrFragment.getCustomProperty( '$rawContent' ) as string );"," \t\t\t\t} else {"," \t\t\t\t\t// UIElement has its own render() method (see https://github.com/ckeditor/ckeditor5/issues/799).","@@ -745,6 +751,7 @@ export class ViewDomConverter {"," \t * @param options.keepOriginalCase If `false`, node's tag name will be converted to lower case. False by default."," \t * @param options.skipComments If `false`, comment nodes will be converted to `$comment`"," \t * {@link module:engine/view/uielement~ViewUIElement view UI elements}. False by default.","+\t * @param options.skipProcessingInstructions If `false`, processing instruction nodes will be converted to `$processingInstruction`"," \t * @returns Converted node or document fragment or `null` if DOM node is a {@link module:engine/view/filler filler}"," \t * or the given node is an empty text node."," \t */","@@ -755,6 +762,7 @@ export class ViewDomConverter {"," \t\t\twithChildren?: boolean;"," \t\t\tkeepOriginalCase?: boolean;"," \t\t\tskipComments?: boolean;","+\t\t\tskipProcessingInstructions?: boolean;"," \t\t} = {}"," \t): ViewNode | ViewDocumentFragment | null {"," \t\tconst inlineNodes: Array<ViewNode> = [];","@@ -1427,6 +1435,7 @@ export class ViewDomConverter {"," \t\t\twithChildren?: boolean;"," \t\t\tkeepOriginalCase?: boolean;"," \t\t\tskipComments?: boolean;","+\t\t\tskipProcessingInstructions?: boolean;"," \t\t},"," \t\tinlineNodes: Array<ViewNode>"," \t): IterableIterator<ViewNode | ViewDocumentFragment | null> {","@@ -1447,6 +1456,10 @@ export class ViewDomConverter {"," \t\t\treturn null;"," \t\t}"," ","+\t\tif ( isProcessingInstruction( domNode ) && options.skipProcessingInstructions ) {","+\t\t\treturn null;","+\t\t}","+"," \t\tif ( isText( domNode ) ) {"," \t\t\tif ( isInlineFiller( domNode ) ) {"," \t\t\t\treturn null;","@@ -1515,6 +1528,13 @@ export class ViewDomConverter {"," "," \t\t\t\t\treturn viewElement;"," \t\t\t\t}","+","+\t\t\t\tif ( isProcessingInstruction( domNode ) ) {","+\t\t\t\t\tviewElement._setCustomProperty( '$processingTarget', domNode.target );","+\t\t\t\t\tviewElement._setCustomProperty( '$processingData', domNode.data );","+","+\t\t\t\t\treturn viewElement;","+\t\t\t\t}"," \t\t\t}"," "," \t\t\t// Yield the element first so the flow of nested inline nodes is not reversed inside elements.","@@ -1857,6 +1877,10 @@ export class ViewDomConverter {"," \t\t\treturn new ViewUIElement( this.document, '$comment' );"," \t\t}"," ","+\t\tif ( isProcessingInstruction( node ) ) {","+\t\t\treturn new ViewUIElement( this.document, '$processingInstruction' );","+\t\t}","+"," \t\tconst viewName = options.keepOriginalCase ? ( node as DomElement )